# ADR: Separate agent behavior from workspace transfer

## Status
Accepted.

## Context
The transfer workflow needs reviewed returns and recoverable local edits.
Client-specific files and terminal patterns also need a clear owner as
more agents become candidates for support.

## Decision
Use saved return plans and backups for review, merge, and undo. Keep
client discovery, files, authentication, startup, and observation decoding
inside adapters. Shared status uses source-labeled observations and keeps
process liveness separate from task progress.

## Alternatives considered
Adding more client-name branches would spread client assumptions through
transfer and status code. Treating terminal matches as proof of task state
would overstate the available evidence.

## Consequences
Claude terminal matches are possible input prompts. Missing evidence means
unknown. Client reports remain reports until returned work is verified.
A second test adapter checks the interface, but does not establish support
for Codex or another real client.

## Validation
52 local tests and 13 Docker integration tests passed. Formatting, Clippy,
and whitespace checks passed. An authenticated Claude round trip verified
remote work, local recall, preserved Git staging, undo, and cleanup. One
manual acknowledgment of a gateway notice was required. See the committed
report in docs/testing/2026-09-29-live-handoff.md.
